{"title":"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1(Good_Ol&#39;_Ratios)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1(Good Ol' Ratios)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(CRITICAL_THINKING!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (CRITICAL THINKING!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An amusement park has a collection of scale models, with a ratio of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/8/3c88aaf0f44ba7573a9ca85e8d57a71a45261457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1: 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" />, of buildings and other sights from around the country. The height of the United States Capitol is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/2/9a2815ecb054fadd5031fb990e85e4ec26a00879.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$289$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> feet. What is the height in feet of its duplicate to the nearest whole number?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/9/36920469724324ec28a6defa7d9eb93794460292.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }14\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }15\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }16\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }18\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"398\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1.28Good_Ol.27_Ratios.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1(Good_Ol'_Ratios)\">Solution 1(Good Ol' Ratios)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1(Good Ol&#39; Ratios)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>You can see that since the ratio of real building's heights to the model building's height is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/d/6cdf471763c744b3315cf349c52aa9b2c620743f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1:20$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" />. We also know that the U.S Capitol is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/2/9a2815ecb054fadd5031fb990e85e4ec26a00879.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$289$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> feet in real life, so to find the height of the model, we divide by 20. That gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/8/1f8e5fa876a650aa64517c3211c15719e72cecb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14.45$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> which rounds to 14. Therefore, to the nearest whole number, the duplicate is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/6/a06db33a644506b138335d1a58e58372d332853c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }14}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"67\" height=\"30\" />.  \n</p><p>~avamarora, Nivaar..\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/e/50ef39308b3aaf7326068d06be2fdcd2c2763109.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{289}{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"29\" height=\"37\" /> and round our answer to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/6/a06db33a644506b138335d1a58e58372d332853c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }14}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"67\" height=\"30\" />.\nIt is basically Solution 1 without the ratio calculation. However, Solution 1 is referring further to the problem.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/2/e629036d93b035769d2a0412abe76767e4d63e7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 \\cdot 14 = 280 ,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"104\" height=\"16\" /> and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/7/a27667360cb2d885702e3bd5e1b704ef3dc5f60d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 \\cdot 15 = 300 .$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"14\" /> These are the multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> around <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/3/f53fae2aba59b97e49813b0a770ce250e16b509b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$289 ,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"31\" height=\"16\" /> and the closest one of those is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/0/a00b9427a41346b81f72b9d765b145c6b9e38b56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$280.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" /> Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/8/068db7dd6b8fb44f67972131defac1b3544dff97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac {280} {20} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }14} .$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"124\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28CRITICAL_THINKING.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(CRITICAL_THINKING!!!)\">Video Solution (CRITICAL THINKING!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (CRITICAL THINKING!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/zF5PqNpI0RM\">https://youtu.be/zF5PqNpI0RM</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/rRaMWpifJJE\">https://youtu.be/rRaMWpifJJE</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8\" title=\"2018 AMC 8\">2018 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2018\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Problem</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?t